{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/pulls/25144","id":5039444391,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAPgMkM8AAAABLF_Rpw","html_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/pull/25144","diff_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/pull/25144.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RobotLocomotion/drake/pull/25144.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/issues/25144","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/pulls/25144/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/pulls/25144/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/issues/25144/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/statuses/f77d3d6d8bce599ece27319b258f83db170063e2","number":25144,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[geometry] Make BoxBoxGradient robust to imprecise witness points","user":{"login":"cohnt","id":24857950,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODU3OTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24857950?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt","html_url":"https://github.com/cohnt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cohnt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #21675.\n\nBoxBoxGradient() demanded that the witness points coincide within 1e-14, but its caller only checks that the signed distance is within 1e-14 of zero, so barely penetrating boxes aborted. This drops that demand. Without it, touching boxes far from the origin, where rounding exceeds the tolerances used to identify the touching feature, can reach the end of the function, so it now returns the axis of minimum overlap there instead of reaching DRAKE_UNREACHABLE. That axis is the correct gradient for any small penetration, and a rounding issue shouldn't abort an optimizer or simulation.\n\nLoosening the demand's tolerance is an alternative, but the rounding error in the witness points is relative to the magnitude of the coordinates, while the check is absolute. No fixed tolerance would hold for boxes far from the origin, so I suggest removing the demand instead. A tolerance scaled to the coordinates would only re-check the caller's distance test, and it wouldn't catch bad FCL output either: in #21947 (since fixed in FCL), wrong witness points passed the demand and failed later.\n\n<!-- Reviewable:start -->\n- - -\nThis change is [<img src=\"https://reviewable.io/review_button.svg\" height=\"34\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"Reviewable\"/>](https://reviewable.io/reviews/RobotLocomotion/drake/25144)\n<!-- Reviewable:end -->\n","labels":[{"id":3420671474,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAPgMkM7L403y","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RobotLocomotion/drake/labels/release%20notes:%20fix","name":"release notes: fix","description":"This pull request contains fixes (no new features)","color":"964B00","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:54:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T20:55:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b7a75760ab1434c8b216fbe416acc64ae2e510b2","assignee":{"login":"SeanCurtis-TRI","id":22159799,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTU5Nzk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22159799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https:/